# Refactored Checkout Service Using Strategy Pattern

## Architecture Overview

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                        CheckoutService                          │
│  Orchestrates: Pricing → Payment → Notification                 │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                              │
        ┌─────────────────────┼─────────────────────┐
        │                     │                     │
        ▼                     ▼                     ▼
┌─────────────────┐  ┌─────────────────┐  ┌─────────────────┐
│ PricingStrategy │  │ PaymentStrategy │  │NotificationStrategy│
│  (VIP, Wholesale│  │ (Stripe, Crypto │  │ (Email, SMS,     │
│   Standard)     │  │  Invoice)       │  │  Webhook)        │
└─────────────────┘  └─────────────────┘  └─────────────────┘
```

## Implementation

```typescript
// ==================== TYPES ====================

export interface Customer {
  id: string;
  email: string;
  phone?: string;
  webhookUrl?: string;
  tier: CustomerTier;
}

export type CustomerTier = 'VIP' | 'WHOLESALE' | 'STANDARD';

export interface CartItem {
  id: string;
  name: string;
  price: number;
  quantity: number;
}

export interface Cart {
  id: string;
  customerId: string;
  items: CartItem[];
}

export interface CheckoutResult {
  total: number;
  status: 'completed' | 'pending' | 'failed';
  transactionId?: string;
  notificationId?: string;
  timestamp: Date;
}

// ==================== PRICING STRATEGY ====================

export interface PricingStrategy {
  calculateTotal(cart: Cart): number;
  getDiscountPercentage(): number;
  getTierName(): CustomerTier;
}

class VipPricingStrategy implements PricingStrategy {
  private readonly discountPercentage = 0.2; // 20% discount

  calculateTotal(cart: Cart): number {
    return cart.items.reduce((total, item) => {
      const discountedPrice = item.price * (1 - this.discountPercentage);
      return total + discountedPrice * item.quantity;
    }, 0);
  }

  getDiscountPercentage(): number {
    return this.discountPercentage;
  }

  getTierName(): CustomerTier {
    return 'VIP';
  }
}

class WholesalePricingStrategy implements PricingStrategy {
  private readonly discountPercentage = 0.35; // 35% discount

  calculateTotal(cart: Cart): number {
    return cart.items.reduce((total, item) => {
      const discountedPrice = item.price * (1 - this.discountPercentage);
      return total + discountedPrice * item.quantity;
    }, 0);
  }

  getDiscountPercentage(): number {
    return this.discountPercentage;
  }

  getTierName(): CustomerTier {
    return 'WHOLESALE';
  }
}

class StandardPricingStrategy implements PricingStrategy {
  private readonly discountPercentage = 0; // No discount

  calculateTotal(cart: Cart): number {
    return cart.items.reduce((total, item) => {
      return total + item.price * item.quantity;
    }, 0);
  }

  getDiscountPercentage(): number {
    return this.discountPercentage;
  }

  getTierName(): CustomerTier {
    return 'STANDARD';
  }
}

export class PricingStrategyFactory {
  private static readonly strategies: Map<CustomerTier, PricingStrategy> = new Map([
    ['VIP', new VipPricingStrategy()],
    ['WHOLESALE', new WholesalePricingStrategy()],
    ['STANDARD', new StandardPricingStrategy()],
  ]);

  static getStrategy(tier: CustomerTier): PricingStrategy {
    const strategy = this.strategies.get(tier);
    if (!strategy) {
      throw new Error(`Unknown customer tier: ${tier}`);
    }
    return strategy;
  }

  static registerStrategy(tier: CustomerTier, strategy: PricingStrategy): void {
    this.strategies.set(tier, strategy);
  }
}

// ==================== PAYMENT STRATEGY ====================

export interface PaymentStrategy {
  processPayment(amount: number): Promise<PaymentResult>;
  getPaymentType(): PaymentType;
  validatePayment(amount: number): boolean;
}

export interface PaymentResult {
  success: boolean;
  transactionId: string;
  message: string;
  timestamp: Date;
}

export type PaymentType = 'stripe' | 'crypto' | 'invoice';

class StripePaymentStrategy implements PaymentStrategy {
  private readonly apiEndpoint = 'https://api.stripe.com/v1/charges';

  async processPayment(amount: number): Promise<PaymentResult> {
    const transactionId = `stripe_${Date.now()}_${Math.random().toString(36).substr(2, 9)}`;

    // Simulate API call
    console.log(`Charging via Stripe credit card API: $${amount.toFixed(2)}`);

    return {
      success: true,
      transactionId,
      message: 'Payment processed successfully via Stripe',
      timestamp: new Date(),
    };
  }

  getPaymentType(): PaymentType {
    return 'stripe';
  }

  validatePayment(amount: number): boolean {
    return amount > 0 && amount < 1000000; // Max $1M per transaction
  }
}

class CryptoPaymentStrategy implements PaymentStrategy {
  private readonly blockchain = 'Solana';

  async processPayment(amount: number): Promise<PaymentResult> {
    const transactionId = `sol_${Date.now()}_${Math.random().toString(36).substr(2, 9)}`;

    // Simulate blockchain transaction
    console.log(`Generating ${this.blockchain} pay transaction for: $${amount.toFixed(2)}`);

    return {
      success: true,
      transactionId,
      message: `Payment initiated on ${this.blockchain} network`,
      timestamp: new Date(),
    };
  }

  getPaymentType(): PaymentType {
    return 'crypto';
  }

  validatePayment(amount: number): boolean {
    return amount > 0 && amount < 500000; // Max $500K for crypto
  }
}

class InvoicePaymentStrategy implements PaymentStrategy {
  private readonly paymentTerms = 'Net-30';

  async processPayment(amount: number): Promise<PaymentResult> {
    const transactionId = `inv_${Date.now()}_${Math.random().toString(36).substr(2, 9)}`;

    // Simulate invoice generation
    console.log(`Generating ${this.paymentTerms} invoice PDF for: $${amount.toFixed(2)}`);

    return {
      success: true,
      transactionId,
      message: `Invoice generated with ${this.paymentTerms} terms`,
      timestamp: new Date(),
    };
  }

  getPaymentType(): PaymentType {
    return 'invoice';
  }

  validatePayment(amount: number): boolean {
    return amount > 0 && amount < 10000000; // Max $10M for invoices
  }
}

export class PaymentStrategyFactory {
  private static readonly strategies: Map<PaymentType, PaymentStrategy> = new Map([
    ['stripe', new StripePaymentStrategy()],
    ['crypto', new CryptoPaymentStrategy()],
    ['invoice', new InvoicePaymentStrategy()],
  ]);

  static getStrategy(paymentType: PaymentType): PaymentStrategy {
    const strategy = this.strategies.get(paymentType);
    if (!strategy) {
      throw new Error(`Unknown payment type: ${paymentType}`);
    }
    return strategy;
  }

  static registerStrategy(paymentType: PaymentType, strategy: PaymentStrategy): void {
    this.strategies.set(paymentType, strategy);
  }
}

// ==================== NOTIFICATION STRATEGY ====================

export interface NotificationStrategy {
  send(customer: Customer, context: NotificationContext): Promise<NotificationResult>;
  getNotificationType(): NotificationType;
  validateCustomer(customer: Customer): boolean;
}

export interface NotificationContext {
  orderId: string;
  total: number;
  timestamp: Date;
}

export interface NotificationResult {
  success: boolean;
  notificationId: string;
  message: string;
  timestamp: Date;
}

export type NotificationType = 'email' | 'sms' | 'webhook';

class EmailNotificationStrategy implements NotificationStrategy {
  private readonly smtpServer = 'smtp.example.com';

  async send(customer: Customer, context: NotificationContext): Promise<NotificationResult> {
    const notificationId = `email_${Date.now()}_${Math.random().toString(36).substr(2, 9)}`;

    console.log(`Sending email confirmation to ${customer.email}`);

    return {
      success: true,
      notificationId,
      message: `Email sent to ${customer.email}`,
      timestamp: new Date(),
    };
  }

  getNotificationType(): NotificationType {
    return 'email';
  }

  validateCustomer(customer: Customer): boolean {
    return customer.email !== undefined && customer.email.includes('@');
  }
}

class SmsNotificationStrategy implements NotificationStrategy {
  private readonly smsProvider = 'Twilio';

  async send(customer: Customer, context: NotificationContext): Promise<NotificationResult> {
    if (!customer.phone) {
      throw new Error('Customer phone number is required for SMS notifications');
    }

    const notificationId = `sms_${Date.now()}_${Math.random().toString(36).substr(2, 9)}`;

    console.log(`Sending SMS to ${customer.phone}`);

    return {
      success: true,
      notificationId,
      message: `SMS sent to ${customer.phone}`,
      timestamp: new Date(),
    };
  }

  getNotificationType(): NotificationType {
    return 'sms';
  }

  validateCustomer(customer: Customer): boolean {
    return customer.phone !== undefined && customer.phone.length >= 10;
  }
}

class WebhookNotificationStrategy implements NotificationStrategy {
  private readonly timeout = 5000;

  async send(customer: Customer, context: NotificationContext): Promise<NotificationResult> {
    if (!customer.webhookUrl) {
      throw new Error('Customer webhook URL is required for webhook notifications');
    }

    const notificationId = `webhook_${Date.now()}_${Math.random().toString(36).substr(2, 9)}`;

    console.log(`POSTing to customer webhook URL ${customer.webhookUrl}`);

    return {
      success: true,
      notificationId,
      message: `Webhook sent to ${customer.webhookUrl}`,
      timestamp: new Date(),
    };
  }

  getNotificationType(): NotificationType {
    return 'webhook';
  }

  validateCustomer(customer: Customer): boolean {
    return customer.webhookUrl !== undefined && customer.webhookUrl.startsWith('http');
  }
}

export class NotificationStrategyFactory {
  private static readonly strategies: Map<NotificationType, NotificationStrategy> = new Map([
    ['email', new EmailNotificationStrategy()],
    ['sms', new SmsNotificationStrategy()],
    ['webhook', new WebhookNotificationStrategy()],
  ]);

  static getStrategy(notificationType: NotificationType): NotificationStrategy {
    const strategy = this.strategies.get(notificationType);
    if (!strategy) {
      throw new Error(`Unknown notification type: ${notificationType}`);
    }
    return strategy;
  }

  static registerStrategy(notificationType: NotificationType, strategy: NotificationStrategy): void {
    this.strategies.set(notificationType, strategy);
  }
}

// ==================== CHECKOUT SERVICE ====================

export class CheckoutService {
  private readonly pricingFactory = PricingStrategyFactory;
  private readonly paymentFactory = PaymentStrategyFactory;
  private readonly notificationFactory = NotificationStrategyFactory;

  async process(
    customer: Customer,
    cart: Cart,
    paymentType: PaymentType,
    notifyType: NotificationType
  ): Promise<CheckoutResult> {
    const startTime = new Date();

    try {
      // 1. Calculate pricing using strategy
      const pricingStrategy = this.pricingFactory.getStrategy(customer.tier);
      const total = pricingStrategy.calculateTotal(cart);

      // 2. Process payment using strategy
      const paymentStrategy = this.paymentFactory.getStrategy(paymentType);

      if (!paymentStrategy.validatePayment(total)) {
        return {
          total,
          status: 'failed',
          timestamp: startTime,
        };
      }

      const paymentResult = await paymentStrategy.processPayment(total);

      if (!paymentResult.success) {
        return {
          total,
          status: 'failed',
          timestamp: startTime,
        };
      }

      // 3. Send notification using strategy
      const notificationStrategy = this.notificationFactory.getStrategy(notifyType);

      if (!notificationStrategy.validateCustomer(customer)) {
        return {
          total,
          status: 'pending',
          transactionId: paymentResult.transactionId,
          timestamp: startTime,
        };
      }

      const notificationResult = await notificationStrategy.send(customer, {
        orderId: paymentResult.transactionId,
        total,
        timestamp: startTime,
      });

      return {
        total,
        status: 'completed',
        transactionId: paymentResult.transactionId,
        notificationId: notificationResult.notificationId,
        timestamp: startTime,
      };

    } catch (error) {
      console.error('Checkout processing error:', error);
      return {
        total: 0,
        status: 'failed',
        timestamp: startTime,
      };
    }
  }
}

// ==================== USAGE EXAMPLE ====================

async function main(): Promise<void> {
  const customer: Customer = {
    id: 'cust_123',
    email: 'customer@example.com',
    phone: '+1234567890',
    webhookUrl: 'https://api.example.com/webhooks/checkout',
    tier: 'VIP',
  };

  const cart: Cart = {
    id: 'cart_456',
    customerId: customer.id,
    items: [
      { id: 'item_1', name: 'Product A', price: 100, quantity: 2 },
      { id: 'item_2', name: 'Product B', price: 50, quantity: 1 },
    ],
  };

  const checkoutService = new CheckoutService();

  const result = await checkoutService.process(
    customer,
    cart,
    'stripe',
    'email'
  );

  console.log('Checkout Result:', result);
}

main();
```

## Refactoring Decisions & Justifications

| Decision | Justification |
|----------|---------------|
| **Strategy Pattern for Each Concern** | Separates pricing, payment, and notification logic into independent, swappable strategies. Each strategy encapsulates its own behavior and can be modified without affecting others. |
| **Factory Pattern for Strategy Selection** | Centralizes strategy instantiation and provides a clean API for retrieving strategies. Makes it easy to add new strategies without modifying existing code (Open/Closed Principle). |
| **Explicit TypeScript Interfaces** | Replaces `any` with strongly typed interfaces. Improves type safety, IDE support, and reduces runtime errors. |
| **Async/Await for I/O Operations** | Payment and notification operations are typically asynchronous. Using `async/await` makes the code more readable and maintainable than callbacks or promises. |
| **Validation in Each Strategy** | Each strategy validates its own requirements (e.g., SMS requires phone, webhook requires URL). This keeps validation logic close to where it's used. |
| **Error Handling in CheckoutService** | Centralized error handling ensures consistent error responses and prevents unhandled exceptions from crashing the checkout flow. |
| **Immutable Strategy Instances** | Strategies are created once and reused (singleton-like via factory). This improves performance and ensures consistent behavior. |
| **Result Objects with Status** | Returns structured results with status, IDs, and timestamps. Makes it easier to track and debug checkout flows. |
| **Extensible Design** | New pricing tiers, payment methods, or notification types can be added by implementing the interface and registering with the factory—no changes to existing code required. |

## Benefits of This Refactoring

1. **Single Responsibility Principle**: Each class has one reason to change.
2. **Open/Closed Principle**: Open for extension, closed for modification.
3. **Testability**: Each strategy can be unit tested independently.
4. **Maintainability**: Changes to one concern don't affect others.
5. **Scalability**: Easy to add new strategies without code duplication.
6. **Type Safety**: Full TypeScript typing eliminates runtime type errors.

